{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"InnoRouterTesting"}],"title":"Event Stream Backpressure"},"sections":[],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NavigationStore"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ModalStore"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FlowStore"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SceneStore"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"publishes an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events: AsyncStream"},{"type":"text","text":" that fans every observation event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out to every subscriber. The fan-out is implemented as a per-subscriber"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream.Continuation"},{"type":"text","text":", which means a slow or cancelled subscriber"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that never drains its stream would otherwise retain every event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indefinitely — behaving as an unbounded leak when the broadcaster"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"outlives all consumers."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To bound that growth, every store accepts an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventBufferingPolicy"},{"text":" in its configuration.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Default policy","anchor":"Default-policy","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventBufferingPolicy.default"},{"type":"text","text":", which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".bufferingNewest(1024)"},{"type":"text","text":". The number is sized for realistic navigation"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bursts (a few hundred events for the longest deep-link replay we have"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measured) while keeping the retained working set bounded so a stuck"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subscriber cannot balloon memory in production."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Choosing a policy","anchor":"Choosing-a-policy","type":"heading","level":2},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Policy","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Behaviour","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When to use"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".bufferingNewest(N)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Retain at most ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N"},{"text":" most-recently-broadcast events per subscriber, dropping older events when the buffer fills.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Production code that prefers loss-of-history over memory growth under contention. The default."}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".bufferingOldest(N)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Retain at most ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"N"},{"text":" oldest-broadcast events per subscriber, dropping newer events when the buffer fills.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Audit pipelines that care about the "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"first"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" burst more than the latest tail (rare)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":".unbounded","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Buffer every event until the subscriber drains it."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Test harnesses or short-lived subscribers where you control lifetime and require deterministic, lossless ordering."}]}]]],"type":"table"},{"text":"Configuring per store","anchor":"Configuring-per-store","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The policy is set per store at construction time via its configuration:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let store = try NavigationStore<HomeRoute>(","    initialPath: [.list],","    configuration: NavigationStoreConfiguration(","        eventBufferingPolicy: .bufferingNewest(2048)","    )",")"],"syntax":"swift skip doc-fragment","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Modal and Flow stores expose the same knob, with one policy per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"published stream:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"NavigationStoreConfiguration.eventBufferingPolicy","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ModalStoreConfiguration.eventBufferingPolicy"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FlowStoreConfiguration.eventBufferingPolicy"},{"type":"text","text":" for the flow-level"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FlowStore.events"},{"type":"text","text":" fan-out"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"FlowStoreConfiguration.navigation.eventBufferingPolicy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"FlowStoreConfiguration.modal.eventBufferingPolicy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for the wrapped"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inner store streams"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Drop-semantics-under-load","level":2,"text":"Drop semantics under load"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Under sustained backpressure, the store keeps emitting events. Whether","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the event reaches a slow subscriber depends on the policy chosen for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that subscriber’s store:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".bufferingNewest(N)"},{"type":"text","text":": oldest events are dropped silently. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subscriber sees a contiguous tail of the most recent N events the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store emitted."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":".bufferingOldest(N)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": newer events are dropped silently after the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"buffer fills. The subscriber sees the first N events emitted after","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it started subscribing.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unbounded"},{"type":"text","text":": nothing is dropped, but the per-subscriber queue can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"grow without bound while the subscriber falls behind."}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Drops are not surfaced as an event. If your analytics pipeline must"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"distinguish “no event happened” from “an event was buffered out”, use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":".unbounded","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for that subscriber and rely on your own pacing rather"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than the broadcaster."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Lifetime-contract","level":2,"text":"Lifetime contract"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each subscriber owns one ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncStream","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". When the subscriber’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"iterator goes out of scope, ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncStream.Continuation.onTermination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fires and the broadcaster removes that slot from its private","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"continuation storage. When a store releases its broadcaster, that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"storage deinitializes, snapshots any outstanding continuations, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"finishes them outside the broadcaster’s actor-isolated deinitializer.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"As a result, ","type":"text"},{"code":"for await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" loops terminate naturally when their store is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"released - no manual cleanup required.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Related","level":2,"text":"Related"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.core\/documentation\/InnoRouterCore\/Middleware-and-Cancellation"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.core\/documentation\/InnoRouterCore\/Rejection-Reasons"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.core\/documentation\/InnoRouterTesting"],["doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.core\/documentation\/InnoRouterTesting","doc:\/\/com.innosquad.innorouter.docs.core\/documentation\/InnoRouterCore\/InnoRouterCore"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/innoroutercore\/event-stream-backpressure"]}],"abstract":[{"text":"How the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events"},{"text":" stream of every store handles slow or stuck subscribers.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major"